#: src/ostd/a-100-line-hypervisor.md:1
msgid "Example: Writing a Hypervisor in About 100 Lines of Safe Rust"
msgstr ""

#: src/ostd/a-100-line-hypervisor.md:3
msgid ""
"This example demonstrates OSTD's hypervisor support on Intel x86 by "
"implementing a minimal hypervisor entirely in safe Rust."
msgstr ""

#: src/ostd/a-100-line-hypervisor.md:5
msgid ""
"This minimal hypervisor aims at running the following Hello World assembly "
"program in a guest. The guest loops over the `\"Hello World\\n\"` string and "
"writes each character to COM1 via the `out` instruction."
msgstr ""

#: src/ostd/a-100-line-hypervisor.md:9
msgid "# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/ostd/a-100-line-hypervisor.md:32
msgid "\"Hello World\\n\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ostd/a-100-line-hypervisor.md:35
msgid ""
"[RFC-0003](../rfcs/0003-hypervisor-support.md) describes the OSTD support "
"required by this minimal hypervisor. Three core OSTD abstractions provide "
"the kernel with hypervisor capabilities:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ostd/a-100-line-hypervisor.md:38
msgid ""
"`GuestPhysMemSpace` maps guest physical addresses to OSTD-managed frames "
"using EPT."
msgstr ""

#: src/ostd/a-100-line-hypervisor.md:39
msgid "`GuestContext` provides access to the guest CPU state."
msgstr ""

#: src/ostd/a-100-line-hypervisor.md:40
msgid ""
"`GuestMode` provides an interface to run the guest using `GuestContext` and "
"`GuestPhysMemSpace`."
msgstr ""

#: src/ostd/a-100-line-hypervisor.md:42
msgid "The code of this minimal hypervisor is shown below:"
msgstr ""

